      </p>
    </figcaption>
  </figure>
	<p>
    My research asks why languages are the way they are, how they came to be this way, and what this tells us about their users. I study language evolution and change in humans, non-human animals, and machines.
    <br><br>
    I'm a tenure-track professor & Ramón y Cajal fellow at the <a href='https://www.upf.edu' target='_blank'>Universitat Pompeu Fabra</a> in Barcelona, Spain. You can reach me via email at firstname.lastname@upf.edu (English, German, Spanish, or Catalan). 
	</p>
</div><!-- /.blurb -->

